    "report": "# Contract checker scoped review\n\nActor: codex-contract-reviewer; driven_by: agent.\nTarget: C:/Users/27933/.codex/worktrees/architecture-convergence-recovered/ClawX\nBase: bfcf57616b361a12845014b3f054b95e31c4021c\nHEAD: ad021f1c56572ab33292d1a2f31c32db53c994ba\n\nFour actionable P2 findings. Run fixtures from the target repository with\nTEMP=TMP=D:/tmp and: node scripts/contract-check.mjs --fixture <absolute path>\nAll fixtures change source text in memory. No repository files, branch state,\nTask Forest or historical evidence were edited.\n\n## 1. Bound channel arguments are discarded\n\nLocation: scripts/contract-check.mjs:303, 317-328.\nFixtures: preload-bound-channel.json, preload-bound-dynamic-channel.json.\n\n    const boundInvoke = ipcRenderer.invoke.bind(ipcRenderer, 'rogue:bound');\n    boundInvoke('host:invoke');\n\nHEAD exit 0. Actual invoked channel is rogue:bound, with host:invoke as payload.\nThe resolver follows bind but discards bound arguments; the visitor reads the\nlater call's first argument. A nonliteral bound channel also passes.\nConversely preload-bound-valid.json binds host:invoke and supplies an object\npayload, and HEAD incorrectly rejects it as a nonstatic channel (exit 1).\n\nMinimum repair: carry the bound channel with resolved method metadata, or\nexplicitly reject pre-applied arguments if unsupported. Add real-entry fixtures\nfor forbidden, nonliteral and permitted bound channels. The current fixture\nflat-ipc-preload-aliased.json binds only this.\n\n## 2. Dynamic method destructuring loses the known IPC origin\n\nLocation: scripts/contract-check.mjs:309-310.\nFixtures: main-destructure-dynamic.json, preload-destructure-dynamic.json.\n\n    const { ipcMain } = require('electron');\n    const method = ['handle'][0];\n    const { [method]: register } = ipcMain;\n    register.call(ipcMain, 'rogue:dynamic', () => 1);\n\nHEAD exit 0. The equivalent direct ipcMain[method](...) is rejected with\nflat-ipc/non-static-method (control-main-direct-dynamic.json, exit 1).\nbindingName returns null, failing methods.includes, so the known IPC origin\nis lost. The ipcRenderer equivalent also exits 0.\n\nMinimum repair: propagate <unresolved> for BindingElement keys on a known IPC\nreceiver just as for ElementAccessExpression. Add Main and preload fixtures.\n\n## 3. Named-default Electron imports regress from rejection to pass\n\nLocation: scripts/contract-check.mjs:273-277.\nFixture: default-import-named-compare.json.\n\n    import { default as admissionElectron } from 'electron';\n    admissionElectron.ipcMain.handle('rogue:default-import', () => 1);\n\nBase exit 1 (flat-ipc/bypass-registry), HEAD exit 0. isElectron recognizes\nImportClause/NamespaceImport but omits ImportSpecifier with imported name default.\nThe normal default import control is rejected by both versions.\n\nMinimum repair: recognize named-default Electron imports; add Main/preload\nequivalence fixtures.\n\n## 4. Binding sources omit defaults and nested destructuring\n\nLocation: scripts/contract-check.mjs:291-292, 309-310.\nFixtures: default-destructure-compare.json, nested-destructure-compare.json.\n\n    {\n      const { ipcMain = require('electron').ipcMain } = {};\n      ipcMain.handle('rogue:default', () => 1);\n    }\n\nBase exit 1, HEAD exit 0. isIpc only reads the whole declaration's initializer\nand ignores the BindingElement default. Also:\n\n    const { ipcMain: { handle: register } } = require('electron');\n    register.call(require('electron').ipcMain, 'rogue:nested', () => 1);\n\nHEAD exit 0. For the nested method, entry.parent.parent is another BindingElement,\nnot the variable declaration, so its initializer is undefined.\n\nMinimum repair: resolve binding sources through enclosing binding patterns,\naccount for defaults, and preserve known Electron alternatives. Unsupported\nknown IPC bindings must be rejected explicitly. Add fixtures for both forms.\n\n## Evidence and validation\n\n- report.json: unchanged-entry baseline exit 0, 11 probes and agent-driven\n  JavaScript argument/destructuring simulations using an in-memory Electron stub.\n- comparison-report.json: six base/HEAD comparisons. Original base checker and\n  entrypoint helper copied byte-for-byte from git objects to D: only.\n  Both checker versions use current repository inputs. No base worktree created.\n- Read relevant AGENTS/spec/rules, ADMISSION-GATE section 8, full checker,\n  focused tests and fixture classes. These examples fit the declared local\n  alias/destructuring/bind boundary; no reflection or cross-module analysis needed.\n- Focused Vitest: 72 tests, 71 passed, one failure after about 32.99s with\n  STACK_TRACE_ERROR for flat-ipc-preload-computed.json. Targeted retry passed.\n  This is not a single clean 72/72 run.\n- Initial configLoader=runner failed on existing __dirname usage before tests.\n  Default bundling then ran with temp config/cache confined to D:/tmp.\n- No installation, full suite, typecheck or Electron E2E. No product acceptance claim.\n- Assignment aliases explored but excluded from findings as outside static-shape scope.\n- Parallel untracked architecture-review-and-integration.md preserved.\n- Final readback observed parallel integration advance HEAD to c10496860dc73a91865bfd7415826624ff78eb33. Relative to reviewed ad021f1c, the checker only gained knowledgeConnectorsApi facade loading at line 763; IPC parser and focused tests are unchanged. Reproductions above remain bound to the requested ad021f1c candidate; the integrated candidate was not rerun.\n",
